#
# aria2c deliverable — handed in as a binary artifact.
# NOT downloaded. NOT built during a normal IRIS build.
#
# Rebuilt 2026-09-04 from the corresponding source published in
# tools/aria2c-build/ (the same recipe this repository ships for GPLv2 §3),
# against OpenSSL 3.5.8. The previous binaries were built on OpenSSL 3.5.7,
# which Alpine withdrew when 3.5.8 shipped; because OpenSSL is linked
# STATICALLY into aria2c, an OS update cannot patch it, so the ten issues
# fixed in 3.5.8 could only be cleared by rebuilding. None of them looked
# reachable in IRIS's client-only usage (see issue #109), but this was the
# last change window before the client is frozen for Cisco signing.
#
# aria2-next version : 2.5.6
# source pin         : d4971f0e12322e2ffcdb1721911b7d5c6206d0e5
# patches applied    : 4
#   - 0001-getpeers-keys-filter.patch
#   - 0002-fix-uaf-peer-blocklist-disconnect.patch
#   - 0003-fix-pkcs12-chain-type-confusion.patch
#   - 0004-fix-ed2k-iterator-invalidation.patch
#
# tools/get-aria2c.sh verifies the handed-in binary against these
# checksums and FAILS CLOSED on a mismatch, so a stale client cannot
# silently ship. Update this file only when adopting a new build.
66663337b99b3d8e273801999a37820fa18f42713cfab4af57a3caefc957555f  x86_64
